description: |
    The :ref:`/plugins/prepare/install` plugin gained a new ``reboot``
    key (``--reboot WHEN`` on the command line). With ``reboot:
    if-installed``, the guest is rebooted after package installation,
    for example to boot into a freshly installed kernel. The reboot is
    skipped when no package was actually installed, image mode guests
    reuse the reboot performed by the ``bootc`` image switch, and the
    option is not supported on ``local``, ``container`` and ``mock``
    guests. The default is ``never``.
